{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses spoke, etc., in the plains of Moab, etc.</b> There is a fine point to examine: why was it necessary to say <b>in the plains of Moab</b>? And if there were a need for this information, he should have mentioned it at the giving of the command, when it says ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳״ etc.? Perhaps it intends what they of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 22:1), a parable to a shepherd etc. — for when they were in the plains of Moab by the Jordan of Jericho, the guarding of the faithful shepherd was completed and he returned them to the [original] count. And therefore the verse also prefaced at the beginning of the section <b>And it was after the plague</b>, to note that even after the plague had occurred among them, they returned to the original count. And for this reason the verse did not state this matter at the giving of the command from HaShem, for this matter concerns Moses himself, to show that the flock did not suffer loss through him." "And if you will say, but I see that HaShem said to him ״שְׂאוּ אֶת רֹאשׁ״ — his intent in that statement was not to count them, for if they would be found to be lacking many, he would have no claim against Him, for it is not comparable to the parable of the shepherd; rather, HaShem's intent was as they of blessed memory said, a parable to a shepherd into whose flock a wolf entered and killed some etc., and Moses found a way to accomplish his desire at the time he needed to count them. And the verse's saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> in this place, where there is no one for them to say it to, means that he told them the intent alluded to in [the phrase] בְּעַרְבוֹת מוֹאָב — that he wishes to restore them to the [original] count, so that they should know that they did not fall short of their first count through him. Or it further intends that he is counting them by decree of what was said to him from HaShem, and not from his own mind alone is he counting them."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:36.423931939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}